================================================================================
SUMMARY (mac-mini-2026-06-29-S1)
================================================================================
EXACT DECOMPOSITION OF d2(M) -- VERIFIED K=8..12, all M tested:
  d2(M) = -meas{x:|Miss(x)|=1, both far phases in the missing inner sector}
          +meas{x:|Miss(x)|=2, far sectors = Miss(x)}
  Miss(x)={1..6}\{sectors hit by base speeds 1..K-3}.
EXACT FROZEN LIMIT d_inf (tent-overlap integral), all match THM-564:
  K=8: 153/4900   K=9: 5699/352800   K=10: 809/57624
  K=11: 631/57624   K=12: 194633/24893568
R(M)=M(d2-d_inf) UNIFORMLY BOUNDED, sup matches THM-564:
  K=8: 0.735  K=9: 0.572  K=10: 0.591(exact)  K=11: ~0.61  K=12: ~0.43

RIGOROUS UNIFORM BOUND (new): integration-by-parts in theta gives
  c_n(x) = (1/2.pi.i.n) Sum_p J_p(x) e(-2.pi.i.n.theta_p(x)),
J_p(x) the theta-jump sizes (bounded variation in x).  Static jumps -> freq nM,
moving jumps (theta=q/7-x) -> freq n(M+1); BV-Fourier gives
  |chat_n(-nM)| <= V_tot/(4.pi^2 n^2 M),  V_tot = Sum_p Var_x(J_p) < infinity,
hence  |R(M)| <= V_tot/12  (M-uniform, explicit, absolutely convergent).
This is the rigorous (loose) cousin of the aspirational 12.zeta(3).N/pi^3.

KEY REFRAME: THM-564 closure needs only SOME finite B with sup|R|<=B; then
M* = ceil((period-max(P)+B)/H_K) is finite and [15,M*] is a finite exact check.
=> Obligation D does NOT require the sharp constant; the finite bound above
   already closes the genuine-wide doublet leg modulo the (already-automated)
   finite window verification.
